@startuml sequence-slides-present
'' PlantUML over Mermaid: presenting is a round trip across the process boundary — a key in the renderer, a
'' request over the IPC seam, a decision in MAIN, the window's own enter/leave event, and the report back — and
'' the point of the design is WHO decides each step (main alone leaves only a fullscreen it entered). A sequence
'' diagram with phase dividers and alt branches states that ordering exactly, and PlantUML takes every participant's
'' colour from the shared theme and renders the SVG byte-reproducibly (README §4). Colours, from the shared palette:
'' magenta = keyboard input and the keymap resolver; blue = re-frame events and effects; blue-violet = app-db;
'' teal = the renderer's views and PDF engine; amber = the IPC seam (every IPC arrow is amber); slate = main and
'' the BrowserWindow it owns.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Presenting (ADR-0045): F5 → window-level fullscreen owned by main → Escape

autonumber "0:"

actor "presenter" as U KEYMAP_TINT
participant "keymap resolver\n(input.resolver ·\nF5 in every :all)" as K KEYMAP_TINT
participant "re-frame events / fx\n(:slides/present · :slides/stop ·\n:input/escape · :view/fullscreen-changed)" as RF REFRAME_TINT
participant "app-db\n[:ui :presentation]\n[:ui :fullscreen?]" as DB APPDB_TINT
participant "views\n(root · pdf-view)" as V RENDERER_TINT
participant "PDF engine\n(renderer.pdf)" as E RENDERER_TINT
participant "preload\nwindow.vv" as P IPC_TINT
participant "main\n(vinary.main.fullscreen)" as M MAIN_TINT
participant "BrowserWindow\n(the sender's window)" as W MAIN_TINT

== F5 — start the show ==
U -[KEYMAP_BORDER]> K : F5
K -> RF : commands/run :slides/present →\n[:slides/present {:from :first}]
activate RF
RF -> RF : slides-present-fx: a PDF is shown,\nno show is running
RF -> DB : [:ui :presentation] ← {:active? true :tab-id :path\n:from :first :fullscreen? true}; clear a typed\nnumber and a blanking
RF -> V : [:dom/focus :content]
RF -[IPC_BORDER]> P : [:vv/set-fullscreen {:on true}]\n(only when :slides-fullscreen? is on)
deactivate RF
P -[IPC_BORDER]> M : **vv:set-fullscreen** {on: true}
activate M
M -> M : BrowserWindow.fromWebContents(sender) —\nonly the requesting window;\ndecide {want? yes, is? no} → {set true, owned true}
M -> W : setFullScreen(true)
deactivate M
DB --> V : :slides/presenting? → .vv-root.vv-presenting\n(CSS hides the menu bar, sidebar, tabs, address bar,\nbottom bar and status bar; the slide sits on black)
V -> E : pdf/update! {:presenting? true :present-from :first}
activate E
E -> E : set-layout! :slides when needed (the page is kept);\nrelayout with no margin; go-to-page! 0;\nattach click-advance and idle-pointer listeners
deactivate E
W --> M : 'enter-full-screen'
M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:fullscreen-changed** {fullscreen: true, owned: true}
P -> RF : [:view/fullscreen-changed …]
RF -> DB : [:ui :fullscreen?] ← true
W -> E : the window grew: the ResizeObserver resizes the slots\nat once (canvases CSS-stretched) and re-renders\nthem sharp 120 ms later

== during the show (the state diagram has the details) ==
U -[KEYMAP_BORDER]> K : → · Space · Shift+→ · digits + Enter · b / w · Tab · a click
note over K, E #E3F2ED
  a slide step runs at once inside the key handler (commands/dispatch-now! →
  scroll delegate → renderer.pdf/step!); a blanked screen or a half-typed number
  goes through [:slides/command] first, which only unblanks / forgets the digits
end note

== Escape — end the show ==
U -[KEYMAP_BORDER]> K : Escape
K -> RF : [:input/escape]
activate RF
RF -> RF : escape-fx, first match: palette? find bar?\noverview? typed number? blanking? — none,\nso the show itself → [:slides/stop]
RF -> DB : dissoc [:ui :presentation]; clear a blanking
RF -[IPC_BORDER]> P : [:vv/set-fullscreen {:on false}]\n(the show had asked for fullscreen)
deactivate RF
P -[IPC_BORDER]> M : **vv:set-fullscreen** {on: false}
activate M
alt main entered this fullscreen (owned)
  M -> M : decide {want? no, is? yes, owned? yes}\n→ {set false, owned false}
  M -> W : setFullScreen(false)
  W --> M : 'leave-full-screen' → owned := false
  M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:fullscreen-changed** {fullscreen: false, owned: false}
else the user had made the window fullscreen before the show
  M -> M : decide {want? no, is? yes, owned? no}\n→ {set nil}: leave the window alone
  M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:fullscreen-changed** {fullscreen: true, owned: false}
end
deactivate M
DB --> V : .vv-presenting removed — the chrome is back
V -> E : pdf/update! {:presenting? false}: the 16 px margin returns;\nthe layout returns to this view's own (its choice, or detection);\nthe presenting-only listeners are detached

== the window leaves fullscreen first (F11, the window manager) ==
U -[MAIN_BORDER]> W : F11
W --> M : 'leave-full-screen' → owned := false
M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:fullscreen-changed** {fullscreen: false, owned: false}
P -> RF : [:view/fullscreen-changed …]
RF -> RF : fullscreen-changed-fx: the window WAS fullscreen,\nthe show asked for it, and now it is not →\nslides-stop-fx {:fullscreen-gone? true}
RF -> DB : dissoc [:ui :presentation] — and no :vv/set-fullscreen\n(there is no fullscreen left to leave)

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#BC6EC5>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| keyboard input, keymap resolver |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame events / effects |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| app-db state |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| renderer: views, PDF engine |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| IPC seam (preload, vv:* channels) |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| main: the fullscreen decision, the BrowserWindow |
  A document's /PageMode /FullScreen never reaches this path: it is deck evidence only.
endlegend
@enduml
